> Data, provenance and exploratory analysis

CIFAR-10 contains 60,000 RGB images at 32 by 32 pixels, grouped into airplane, automobile, bird, cat, deer, dog, frog, horse, ship and truck. There are 5,000 official training and 1,000 official test images per class. The five training files have a random class mix; concatenating all five is necessary for the intended training population. The original source is [Krizhevsky, Nair and Hinton's dataset page|https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html], with the associated 2009 technical report, *Learning Multiple Layers of Features from Tiny Images*.

Acquisition uses `dm::datasets::fetch("cifar10")` and the shared configurable cache. The native fetcher pins the binary archive MD5 to `c32a1d4ab5d03f1284b67883e8d87530`; existing extracted caches are reused. Therefore this study also records and checks SHA-256 fingerprints of all six binary files in `artifacts/dataset.sha256`. These are fingerprints of the actual inputs used here, not a claim that a pre-existing cache was downloaded again. The binary reader requires complete records. Labels and class supports are checked, and archived split IDs are verified to form a disjoint complete partition.

RGB statistics below are computed only from fitting pixels, with Float64 population-moment reductions. The standardised input is `(pixel - fitting_mean) / fitting_sd`. Validation and test data never determine these moments.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/cifar10_study.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/classification_analysis.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <map>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace s = n::study;
  n::set_num_threads(8);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const bool rebuilding = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_CIFAR10_RETRAIN") &&
                          std::string(std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_CIFAR10_RETRAIN")) == "1";
  const auto data = rebuilding || !std::filesystem::exists("artifacts/preprocessing.npz")
                        ? s::prepare_cifar10()
                        : s::restore_cifar10_study("artifacts/preprocessing.npz");
  if (rebuilding || !std::filesystem::exists("artifacts/preprocessing.npz")) {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("artifacts");
    n::save_npz(
        "artifacts/preprocessing.npz",
        {{"mean", data.mean},
         {"sd", data.sd},
         {"fit_ids", n::from_vector(data.fit_ids, {45000})},
         {"validation_ids", n::from_vector(data.validation_ids, {5000})}});
  }
  std::ofstream("build/dataset_directory.txt") << data.directory << '\n';
  std::print(
      "| Partition | Images | Images per class | Purpose |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n"
      "| Fitting | {} | 4500 | Gradients and RGB moments |\n"
      "| Validation | {} | 500 | Rate, checkpoint and temperature |\n"
      "| Official test | 10000 | 1000 | Frozen evaluation |\n",
      data.fit.labels.numel(),
      data.validation.labels.numel());
  std::print("\n| Channel | Fitting mean | Fitting population SD |\n|---|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c)
    std::print(
        "| {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",
        std::vector<std::string>{"Red", "Green", "Blue"}[c],
        data.mean.at({c}),
        data.sd.at({c}));
}
