| Partition pair | Exact matching image pairs |
|---|---:|
| Fitting / Fitting | 0 |
| Fitting / Validation | 0 |
| Fitting / Official test | 0 |
| Validation / Validation | 0 |
| Validation / Official test | 0 |
| Official test / Official test | 0 |

0 validation images and 0 test images exactly match fitting pixels. Across all partitions, 0 matching-image pairs carry conflicting labels.
After excluding test images with exact fitting matches: N=10000, accuracy 0.9021, calibrated NLL 0.30200. This is a post-fit sensitivity analysis; official benchmark scores retain all images.
// result_end
\caption(Exact decoded-image overlap, conflicting annotation pairs and a frozen-score sensitivity check.)

The native evaluation above reopens the frozen checkpoint and recomputes the logits. The following tables and figures consume the saved per-image results; they do not refit or select the model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/cifar10_study.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/classification_analysis.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <map>
#include <sstream>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("artifacts/evaluation.npz"))
    a[k] = v;
  std::ifstream in("artifacts/scores.tsv");
  std::string   line;
  std::getline(in, line);
  std::print(
      "| Evaluation | Temperature | Accuracy | NLL | Brier | ECE (15 bins) "
      "|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  while (std::getline(in, line)) {
    std::istringstream r(line);
    std::string        name;
    double             t, acc, nll, brier, ece;
    r >> name >> t >> acc >> nll >> brier >> ece;
    std::print(
        "| {} | {:.4f} | {:.4f} | {:.5f} | {:.5f} | {:.5f} |\n", name, t, acc, nll, brier, ece);
  }
  const auto c  = n::ConfusionMatrix::from_counts(a.at("confusion"));
  const auto ci = dm::stats::proportion_test_one_sample(std::llround(c.accuracy() * 10000), 10000);
  std::print(
      "\nTest macro F1: {:.5f}; Wilson 95% accuracy interval: [{:.5f}, {:.5f}].\n",
      c.macro().f1,
      ci.conf_int_lower,
      ci.conf_int_upper);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Evaluation | Temperature | Accuracy | NLL | Brier | ECE (15 bins) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| fit | 1.0000 | 0.9939 | 0.01887 | 0.00936 | 0.00504 |
| validation_raw | 1.0000 | 0.9026 | 0.44412 | 0.15776 | 0.06246 |
| validation_calibrated | 2.2789 | 0.9026 | 0.29882 | 0.14193 | 0.00880 |
| test_raw | 1.0000 | 0.9021 | 0.44436 | 0.15832 | 0.06068 |
| test_calibrated | 2.2789 | 0.9021 | 0.30200 | 0.14321 | 0.00571 |

Test macro F1: 0.90209; Wilson 95% accuracy interval: [0.89612, 0.90777].
