\alttext(Selective classification error as progressively less-confident test predictions are included.)

> Correct, incorrect and uncertain predictions

Examples follow fixed selection rules. Correct examples are the first correct official-test observation in each true class. Bad predictions are the ten incorrect observations with the highest calibrated confidence. A third panel shows the ten least confident observations regardless of correctness. Thus the first panel illustrates successful cases, while the second deliberately exposes confident failures; neither is a random accuracy sample. Exact official-test row IDs and labels appear below each panel and in `artifacts/prediction_examples.tsv`.

