> Interpretability: definitions, computation and controls

Explanations target a fixed raw predicted-class logit, not a changing argmax or the calibrated probability. The eight cases are the first correct airplane, automobile, bird and cat examples, followed by the four most confident errors. This intentionally selected set illustrates contrasting outcomes; it is not an estimate of explanation behaviour across all classes.

Grad-CAM uses the actual last post-ReLU stage tensor, of shape 4 by 4 by 128. For class c its channel weights and map are

$$\alpha_k^c=\frac1{16}\sum_{u,v}\frac{\partial z_c}{\partial A_{uvk}},\qquad M^c=\operatorname{ReLU}\left(\sum_k\alpha_k^c A_k\right).$$
\alttext(Grad-CAM spatially averages the class-logit derivative in each channel, weights the last-stage activation maps and rectifies their sum.)

This follows [Selvaraju et al., *Grad-CAM*|https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.02391]. The coarse map is max-normalised per image for display and bilinearly enlarged. Its 4-by-4 support limits localisation: a smooth overlay does not create pixel-level explanatory resolution. Since the head is linear after global average pooling, these gradients also have the expected spatially constant per-channel structure.

Integrated gradients (IG) instead attributes the logit difference from a flat fitting-mean RGB image to the observed image:

$$\operatorname{IG}_j(x;x')=(x_j-x'_j)\int_0^1\frac{\partial z_c(x'+\alpha(x-x'))}{\partial x_j}\,d\alpha.$$
\alttext(Each integrated attribution is the input change from a specified baseline times the average ordinary input derivative along the straight path.)

The sum of exact IG contributions equals the raw-logit difference under the usual path regularity assumptions. Finite midpoint quadrature is approximate, so this study retains results at 128, 256 and 512 nodes and reports signed completeness residuals. Path coordinates and derivative accumulation use Float64; the actual model evaluates Float32 inputs. A second 512-node computation uses a black baseline to expose baseline dependence. This follows [Sundararajan, Taly and Yan, *Axiomatic Attribution for Deep Networks*|https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.01365].

Occlusion replaces each 8-by-8 patch by fitting-mean RGB, with stride four. Forty-nine patches cover the full image. The recorded quantity is original target logit minus occluded target logit; negative values mean replacement increased that score. Overlap averaging produces a display map. This finite intervention follows the occlusion approach of [Zeiler and Fergus, *Visualizing and Understanding Convolutional Networks*|https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.2901]. It is neither an additive pixel attribution nor a causal object mask.

Two controls qualify interpretation. A randomly reinitialised classifier head tests whether a normalised Grad-CAM map changes when class evidence changes while features remain fixed. A separate deletion check replaces the four non-overlapping 8-by-8 blocks with greatest summed absolute IG magnitude (25% of pixels), and compares the target-score drop with four uniformly shuffled blocks of the same size. There is one seeded random deletion per selected case, so this is a local diagnostic rather than a statistical faithfulness benchmark. Both interventions may move inputs off the natural-image distribution.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/cifar10_study.hpp>
#include <fstream>
#include <iomanip>
#include <iostream>
#include <map>

int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  namespace s = n::study;
  n::set_num_threads(8);
  const auto run = n::read_csv("artifacts/training_summary.tsv", nullptr, true, '\t');
  if (run.shape() != n::Shape{1, 8} || run.at({0, 6}) != 1)
    throw std::runtime_error("complete converged training before test computations");
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> saved;
  for (const auto& [name, value] : n::load_npz("artifacts/evaluation.npz"))
    saved[name] = value;
  const auto data    = s::restore_cifar10_study("artifacts/preprocessing.npz");
  const auto test    = n::load_cifar10(data.directory, "test");
  const auto ids     = saved.at("explain_ids").to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  const auto x       = n::take_rows(test.images, ids);
  const auto targets = n::argmax(n::take_rows(saved.at("test_logits"), ids), 1).to(n::DType::Int32);
  const auto selector = n::one_hot(targets, 10, 1, 0, n::DType::Float32);
  const auto baseline = n::ones_like(x) * data.mean; // Flat fitting-mean RGB image.
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    m::ResNet(p, state, n::zeros({1, 32, 32, 3}), s::cifar10_resnet_config(), false);
  }
  p.load("artifacts/best_parameters.npz");
  state.load("artifacts/best_bn.npz");
  auto predict = [&](const n::Tensor& images) {
    return s::cifar10_logits(p, state, images, data.mean, data.sd, 64);
  };
  m::InputGradientFunction gradient = [&](const n::Tensor& points, const n::Tensor& target) {
    const auto input = points.detach().requires_grad_();
    const auto z     = m::ResNet(
                       p,
                       state,
                       s::standardize_cifar10(input, data.mean, data.sd),
                       s::cifar10_resnet_config(),
                       false)
                       .logits;
    const auto score = n::sum(z * n::one_hot(target, 10, 1, 0, n::DType::Float32));
    return n::grad(score, {input})[0].detach();
  };
  auto cam = [&](n::ParameterStore& weights) {
    const auto out = m::ResNet(
        weights,
        state,
        s::standardize_cifar10(x, data.mean, data.sd),
        s::cifar10_resnet_config(),
        false);
    const auto derivative = n::grad(n::sum(out.logits * selector), {out.stages.back()})[0];
    return m::ClassActivationMaps(out.stages.back(), derivative).grad_map.detach();
  };
  const auto coarse_cam = cam(p);
  const auto cam_unit   = m::NormalizeCam(coarse_cam);
  const auto ig128      = m::IntegratedGradients(x, baseline, targets, 128, 32, gradient);
  const auto ig256      = m::IntegratedGradients(x, baseline, targets, 256, 32, gradient);
  const auto ig512      = m::IntegratedGradients(x, baseline, targets, 512, 32, gradient);
  const auto black      = n::zeros_like(x);
  const auto ig_black   = m::IntegratedGradients(x, black, targets, 512, 32, gradient);
  const auto occlusion  = m::OcclusionSensitivity(x, baseline, targets, {8, 8, 4, 4}, 64, predict);
  const auto score      = n::sum(predict(x) * selector, {1});
  const auto delta      = score.to(n::DType::Float64) - n::sum(predict(baseline) * selector, {1}).to(n::DType::Float64);
  auto       completeness = [&](const n::Tensor& attribution) {
    return n::sum(attribution.to(n::DType::Float64), {1, 2, 3}) - delta.to(n::DType::Float64);
  };
  // Head randomisation keeps the feature extractor fixed while changing class evidence.
  auto         randomized = p.clone();
  n::Generator random(991);
  randomized.set("output/W", n::normal(p.at("output/W").shape(), 0, .1, random));
  randomized.set("output/b", n::zeros_like(p.at("output/b")));
  const auto control_cam = m::NormalizeCam(cam(randomized));

  // A separate deletion experiment uses non-overlapping 8x8 blocks, ranked by IG.
  // The random control has the same number, size and replacement distribution.
  const auto importance = n::sum(n::abs(ig512.attribution), {3});
  const auto block_importance =
      n::avg_pool2d(n::expand_dims(importance, 3), 8, 8, n::Padding::Valid)
          .reshape({x.size(0), 16});
  auto       top_mask = n::zeros({x.size(0), 32, 32, 1}), random_mask = n::zeros_like(top_mask);
  const auto yy = n::arange(0, 32, 1, n::DType::Int64).reshape({1, 32, 1, 1});
  const auto xx = n::arange(0, 32, 1, n::DType::Int64).reshape({1, 1, 32, 1});
  for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < x.size(0); ++i) {
    std::vector<int> blocks(16);
    std::iota(blocks.begin(), blocks.end(), 0);
    std::stable_sort(blocks.begin(), blocks.end(), [&](int a, int b) {
      return block_importance.at({i, a}) > block_importance.at({i, b});
    });
    const auto row =
        n::equal(n::arange(0, x.size(0), 1, n::DType::Int64), i).reshape({x.size(0), 1, 1, 1});
    const auto perm = n::permutation(16, random).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
    for (int j = 0; j < 4; ++j) {
      auto mask = [&](int b) {
        return n::cast(row, n::DType::Float32) *
               n::cast(n::greater_equal(yy, (b / 4) * 8), n::DType::Float32) *
               n::cast(n::less(yy, (b / 4 + 1) * 8), n::DType::Float32) *
               n::cast(n::greater_equal(xx, (b % 4) * 8), n::DType::Float32) *
               n::cast(n::less(xx, (b % 4 + 1) * 8), n::DType::Float32);
      };
      top_mask    = top_mask + mask(blocks[j]);
      random_mask = random_mask + mask(perm[j]);
    }
  }
  const auto top_drop =
      score.to(n::DType::Float64) - n::sum(predict(n::where(n::greater(top_mask, 0), baseline, x)) * selector, {1}).to(n::DType::Float64);
  const auto random_drop =
      score.to(n::DType::Float64) - n::sum(predict(n::where(n::greater(random_mask, 0), baseline, x)) * selector, {1}).to(n::DType::Float64);
  n::save_npz(
      "artifacts/explanations.npz",
      {{"ids", saved.at("explain_ids")},
       {"targets", targets},
       {"raw_images", x},
       {"cam_raw", coarse_cam},
       {"cam_normalized", cam_unit},
       {"cam_random_head", control_cam},
       {"ig128", ig128.attribution},
       {"ig256", ig256.attribution},
       {"ig512", ig512.attribution},
       {"ig_black512", ig_black.attribution},
       {"occlusion_pixel", occlusion.pixel_mean},
       {"occlusion_drops", occlusion.drops},
       {"score_difference", delta},
       {"completeness128", completeness(ig128.attribution)},
       {"completeness256", completeness(ig256.attribution)},
       {"completeness512", completeness(ig512.attribution)},
       {"ig_top25_drop", top_drop},
       {"random25_drop", random_drop}});
  std::ofstream checks("artifacts/interpretability.tsv");
  checks << "test_id\ttarget\tscore_difference\tig128_residual\tig256_residual\tig512_"
            "residual\ttop25_drop\trandom25_drop\n"
         << std::setprecision(12);
  const auto e128 = completeness(ig128.attribution), e256 = completeness(ig256.attribution),
             e512 = completeness(ig512.attribution);
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < ids.size(); ++i)
    checks << ids[i] << '\t' << targets.at({static_cast<int64_t>(i)}) << '\t'
           << delta.at({static_cast<int64_t>(i)}) << '\t' << e128.at({static_cast<int64_t>(i)})
           << '\t' << e256.at({static_cast<int64_t>(i)}) << '\t'
           << e512.at({static_cast<int64_t>(i)}) << '\t' << top_drop.at({static_cast<int64_t>(i)})
           << '\t' << random_drop.at({static_cast<int64_t>(i)}) << '\n';
  std::cout << "Computed Grad-CAM, IG at 128/256/512 nodes, two IG baselines, 49 occlusions per "
               "case, and deletion controls for "
            << ids.size() << " fixed cases.\n";
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Computed Grad-CAM, IG at 128/256/512 nodes, two IG baselines, 49 occlusions per case, and deletion controls for 8 fixed cases.
// result_end
\caption(Executed explanation computation with fixed targets, frozen BN and explicit baselines. Raw arrays and all numerical checks are retained in `artifacts/explanations.npz` and `artifacts/interpretability.tsv`.)

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/explanations_correct.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/cifar10_study.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/classification_analysis.hpp>
#include <map>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz("artifacts/explanations.npz"))
    a[k] = v;
  const auto x   = a.at("raw_images"),
             cam = n::resize_bilinear(
                 n::expand_dims(a.at("cam_normalized"), 3), {32, 32}, false, true);
  const auto colour        = n::concat({cam, 1 - n::abs(2 * cam - 1), 1 - cam}, 3);
  const auto overlay       = .55 * x + .45 * colour;
  auto       signed_colour = [](const n::Tensor& map) {
    const auto q = map / n::maximum(n::max(n::abs(map), {1, 2}, true), n::scalar_like(1e-12, map));
    const auto t = n::expand_dims(q, 3);
    return n::concat({1 - n::relu(-t), 1 - n::abs(t), 1 - n::relu(t)}, 3).to(n::DType::Float32);
  };
  const auto             ig  = signed_colour(n::sum(a.at("ig512"), {3}));
  const auto             occ = signed_colour(a.at("occlusion_pixel"));
  std::vector<n::Tensor> tiles;
  for (int64_t i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
    for (const auto& image : {x, overlay, ig, occ})
      tiles.push_back(n::slice_axis(image, 0, i, i + 1));
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(tiles, 0), "build/explanations_correct.png", 4, 0, 1, 2, 1, 5);
  std::print(
      "Rows are the selected correct cases. Columns: original; Grad-CAM overlay; signed RGB-summed "
      "IG; signed occlusion.\n");
}
```
